# novadeck OTA release signing certificate profile — the ONE definition of it.
#
# Read by BOTH ci/gen-signing-ca.sh (which mints the real cert with it) and
# images/rauc/verify-signing.sh (which mints a throwaway cert with it and proves the shipped
# /etc/rauc/system.conf accepts one). It is a file rather than a heredoc in each because it used to
# be a heredoc in each: the self-test carried a hand-copy of these three lines, so a change here
# would have left it passing for a cert profile we no longer ship — a green check asserting the
# wrong thing, which is worse than no check at all.
#
# extendedKeyUsage=codeSigning and CA:FALSE are what stop this cert being usable to mint more certs
# or to terminate TLS if it ever leaks out of CI. That EKU is also why system.conf needs
# check-purpose=codesign: RAUC's default verification purpose is smimesign, which accepts only
# emailProtection or no EKU at all, so the two ends have to be changed together. They are asserted
# to agree by verify-signing.sh, and tests/test-verify-signing.sh asserts that assertion bites.
#
# OpenSSL x509v3 extension format (openssl x509 -req -extfile). Comments are '#'.
basicConstraints=critical,CA:FALSE
keyUsage=critical,digitalSignature
extendedKeyUsage=critical,codeSigning
